Hi Rahul,

During our discussion, you clearly mentioned that you have a business plan
and are also holding two offers, from which you would decide which one to
pursue. You further stated that you expected to finalize one of the offers
within a day or two and raised the possibility that the selected
organization might require you to join within a similar short timeline.

In response to your concern regarding such a situation, I clearly informed
you that we would support you with an early relieving, subject to
completing the necessary handover and transition requirements.

I would also like to clarify that there was no misunderstanding regarding
this discussion. When you specifically raised the request for early
relieving, I reiterated and clarified this with you during the conversation
to ensure a clear understanding on both sides.

Additionally, within a few minutes of the discussion, you yourself
mentioned that you were already prepared for the possibility of such a
notice from the company and had made your plans accordingly. This further
indicated that you had already considered the possibility and were prepared
for the next steps.

Our objective throughout the discussion was to maintain transparency and
provide clarity regarding the situation while ensuring the transition is
handled professionally and in accordance with the organization=E2=80=99s
requirements.
As mentioned you can visit HR to see the documents.


Regards,
